4.67.m:
He engaged in love-play in the jewelled palace;
so the lover [dwelt] with Rādhā, who was full of desire.
Thus ends the sixty-seventh chapter, entitled 'Discourse on Spiritual Yoga', in the Uttara[-khaṇḍa] of the glorious Kṛṣṇajanmakhaṇḍa in the great Śrī Brahmavaivarta Purāṇa, in the dialogue between Nārada and [Nārāyaṇa].
